From: fpvOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: wave5: keep the HEVC refresh band at two CTU rows or more

On the AR9311's WAVE521C (firmware revision 330638) the refreshed band moves
one CTU row a picture whatever the count; the count only sets the band's
width, and a count of 1 refreshes nothing. A period equal to the picture's
CTU rows (17 at 1080p) rounded up to a count of 1, so the stream ran with no
refresh at all: keep the count at 2 or more.

Also check the CTU-row argument against the CTU-row count: the validation
read the H.264 macroblock field.

Upstream: not submitted

--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-hw.c
@@ -2677,7 +2677,7 @@ static bool wave5_vpu_enc_check_common_param_valid(struct vpu_instance *inst,
 	}
 	switch (param->intra_refresh_mode) {
 	case REFRESH_MODE_CTU_ROWS:
-		if (param->intra_mb_refresh_arg > num_ctu_row)
+		if (param->intra_refresh_arg > num_ctu_row)
 			goto invalid_refresh_argument;
 		break;
 	case REFRESH_MODE_CTU_COLUMNS:
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-enc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-enc.c
@@ -1558,9 +1558,16 @@ static int wave5_set_enc_openparam(struct enc_open_param *open_param,
 		/* Firmware refreshes whole CTU rows. Round up so a sweep takes
 		 * no longer than the requested number of pictures, including when
 		 * the requested period exceeds the number of rows.
+		 *
+		 * Measured on the AR9311 firmware (WAVE521C, revision 330638): the
+		 * refreshed band moves one CTU row a picture whatever the count,
+		 * so a 1080p sweep takes 17 pictures; the count only sets the
+		 * band's width, and a count of 1 refreshes nothing. Keep it at 2
+		 * or more where the picture has that many rows.
 		 */
 		open_param->wave_param.intra_refresh_arg =
-			DIV_ROUND_UP(num_ctu_row, input.intra_refresh_arg);
+			max_t(u32, min_t(u32, 2, num_ctu_row),
+			      DIV_ROUND_UP(num_ctu_row, input.intra_refresh_arg));
 	}
 	open_param->wave_param.forced_idr_header_enable = input.forced_idr_header_enable;
 
